3. 992 orphan keys preserved per ADR-005 #1 / Honesty Covenant rule 11. A whole-file regex scan finds 151 of these are actually live multi-line t() references invisible to the line-by-line scanner — pruning them would break translations at runtime.
4. Validator: scripts/i18n-validate-keys.mjs (line-by-line T_CALL + DEFAULT_VALUE_OPT regex). Non-strict mode always exits 0; gate enforces additivity via structural diff against HEAD.
5. PowerShell-7 quirks reused from prior phase-43 prompts:
   (a) Resolve-Path ABSOLUTE on log path BEFORE Push-Location web — else Tee-Object inside web/ fails to find the relative .github/prompts path.
   (b) Use npm.cmd (not npm) under pwsh -File / inline pwsh — npm 10 executable-resolution quirk.
   (c) DO NOT run gate via 'pwsh -File .tmp_gate.ps1' inside the repo root — the untracked script appears in 'git status --porcelain' and trips the disallowed-files check before the script can self-delete. Instead inline the gate body directly OR self-delete the script BEFORE the status check.
6. Manually authored 8 keys whose call sites use ternary, runtime, multi-line, or empty-string fallbacks the validator's static regex cannot capture: Read-Write, layout.editTitle, widget.updateStatus, tempImpact.tipOptimal/optimalDesc/optimalDelta, notifications.alertStudio.computedMetric.would, vehicles.removeMessage.
